From d03ff5db035332e455913fb9772e664e80eb5f71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "MOTOR-43 (Claude)" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 23:06:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ntp: FlyWeb private new tab page without Brave Search or Tor

With BravePrivateNewTabUI back on private and guest windows, the page
showed the Brave Search logo (lion and "brave search"), searched on Brave
Search regardless of the user's default search engine, and its notice
ended by suggesting a private window with Tor, which FlyWeb does not
have.

- Search box: FlyWeb's fly (the new tab page's drawing, copied into this
  bundle with its Trusted Types-safe converter, as brave_welcome_ui does)
  instead of the Brave Search logo; the form's accessible name comes from
  the localized placeholder instead of "Brave".
- GoToBraveSearch becomes GoToSearch and uses the profile's default
  search engine (TemplateURLServiceFactory redirects off-the-record and
  guest profiles to the original one).
- The notice shows only headerText1 (IDS_..._PRIVATE_WINDOW_DESC1). The
  dropped headerText2 mentions Tor in every translation. No string or
  translation file is changed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MwmK2keCUcEPJ6KTcxicZD
